<div class="single-topic-subs-grid">
  <div class="subs-item">
    <h3>Proof for Compliance First</h3>
    <p>Begin with the RFP, not grammar. Verify page limits, fonts, margins, forms, file names, and submission steps. Build a one-page checklist and map responses to exact requirements with matching headings. Confirm every “shall” is answered and easy to find. Grammar and polish come second—non-compliance costs points fast.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="subs-item">
    <h3>Standardize Names, Numbers, and Acronyms</h3>
    <p>Create a mini style sheet (capitalization, hyphenation, acronyms, units, dates). Run targeted searches for double spaces, inconsistent dashes, stray smart quotes, and % spacing. Confirm client/project names, licenses, and dollar figures against source records. Spell out acronyms on first use and keep them consistent throughout.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="subs-item">
    <h3>Two-Pass Method: Story, Then Surface</h3>
    <p>Pass 1: read for logic and flow—do headings promise what paragraphs deliver; do win themes recur; are transitions clear? Pass 2: line-edit in PDF at ~125% zoom to catch wraps, spacing, widows/orphans, and figure/table references. Test links, check callout styles, and export a clean final with controlled file naming.</p>
  </div>
</div>